# Runs stay local so the repo doesn't fill with every sweep. A log that backs a
# reported number is evidence, so it is tracked by name. The 27 Sep dev baseline
# is the one METHODOLOGY sections 4 and 5 cite. Its scored file is tracked too,
# because cli.py report reads scored logs and nothing can re-score a raw one yet.
!logs/run-20260927T082229Z.jsonl
!logs/scored-20260927T082229Z.jsonl
results/*.csv
results/*.json
